# Structural refusal (selftest: must FAIL before rendering): `sotp` and `sto`
# are typos of landing.scad's `stop`. A -D of a name the source never assigns
# binds nothing and OpenSCAD says nothing, so the geometry sits at one pose
# and every check "holds" at every value — the swept/stepped parameter must
# be a top-level assignment of the entry .scad, and both lines must be named.
sweep sotp
empty landing-flat
stops sto 0,1
empty-control landing-flat-rolled
